Steps to execute:

Install Dependencies

Run on both monitoring-vm and aiops-incident-vm:

sudo apt update -y
sudo apt install -y docker.io docker-compose python3 python3-pip sqlite3 curl git
sudo systemctl enable docker && sudo systemctl start docker

Step 3 — Configure Node Exporter (Target VM)
docker run -d --name node-exporter \
  -p 9100:9100 \
  prom/node-exporter


Check it:

curl http://localhost:9100/metrics

 Step 4 — Configure Prometheus (Monitoring VM)

Create file:

vi ~/monitoring/prometheus.yml

global:
  scrape_interval: 15s
scrape_configs:
  - job_name: "prometheus"
    static_configs:
      - targets: ["localhost:9090"]

  - job_name: "node"
    static_configs:
      - targets: ["<TARGET_VM_EXTERNAL_IP>:9100"]

 Step 5 — Add Alert Rules
vi ~/monitoring/alert_rules.yml

groups:
  - name: node_alerts
    rules:
      - alert: NodeExporterDown
        expr: up{job="node"} == 0
        for: 30s
        labels:
          severity: critical
        annotations:
          description: "Node Exporter is down on {{ $labels.instance }}"

 Step 6 — Configure Alertmanager
vi ~/monitoring/alertmanager.yml

global:
  resolve_timeout: 5m

route:
  receiver: 'aiops-bot'

receivers:
  - name: 'aiops-bot'
    webhook_configs:
      - url: 'http://<AIOPS_VM_INTERNAL_IP>:5000/alert'

 Step 7 — Run Prometheus and Alertmanager in Docker
docker run -d --name prometheus \
  -p 9090:9090 \
  -v ~/monitoring/prometheus.yml:/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml \
  -v ~/monitoring/alert_rules.yml:/etc/prometheus/alert_rules.yml \
  prom/prometheus --config.file=/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml

docker run -d --name alertmanager \
  -p 9093:9093 \
  -v ~/monitoring/alertmanager.yml:/etc/alertmanager/alertmanager.yml \
  prom/alertmanager


Check Prometheus UI → http://<monitoring-vm-ip>:9090

 Step 8 — Create Slack App & Webhook

1️ Go to https://api.slack.com/apps

2️ Create → “From scratch” → App name alert → Workspace Intern.
3️ Add Incoming Webhook feature.
 Activate & copy your webhook URL (looks like):

https://hooks.slack.com/services/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


5️ Add this app to your channel (e.g., #all-intern).

 Step 9 — Build the Flask AIOps App (AIOps-Incident VM)
File: ~/aiops-incident/ai_anomaly_insights.py

Step 10 — Run the Flask App
sudo fuser -k 5000/tcp
nohup python3 ~/aiops-incident/ai_anomaly_insights.py > ~/aiops-incident/ai_alerts.log 2>&1 &
tail -f ~/aiops-incident/ai_alerts.log

 Step 11 — Test Webhook
curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{"alerts":[{"labels":{"alertname":"HighCPUUsage"},"annotations":{"description":"CPU usage above 90% on server-prod-01"}}]}' \
http://<AIOPS_VM_EXTERNAL_IP>:5000/alert


